# Handoff

Every workspace keeps three files at the repo root:

- `AGENT_LOG.md` — what was done
- `ROADMAP.md` — what is next
- `AUDIT.md` — how it is built and what is still open

At the start of a session, before answering about the work or editing it, read all three.

If a file is missing, create it before the first change in that repo. A new `AGENT_LOG.md` starts with a heading and one dated section. A new `ROADMAP.md` starts with what is next. A new `AUDIT.md` starts with how the system is built and what is open. If a file already has a shape, match it.

After every task, append a dated entry to `AGENT_LOG.md` and leave older entries in place. Update `ROADMAP.md` when the next work changes. Update `AUDIT.md` when the structure or an open problem changes.

Use these file names. Do not add `MEMORY.md` or `agent_log.md`.
